  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2409.16165",
  "abstract": "EnIGMA is an LM agent designed to solve Capture The Flag (CTF) challenges, which are a type of cybersecurity competition. EnIGMA uses interactive tools and interfaces to improve its ability to find and exploit security vulnerabilities. The agent achieves state-of-the-art results on several benchmarks, including NYU CTF, InterCode-CTF, and CyBench. This paper presents the design and evaluation of EnIGMA, highlighting its ability to adapt to new strategies and solve challenges that were previously unsolvable.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The core idea of EnIGMA is to use <strong>interactive tools and interfaces</strong> to improve the ability of LM agents to find and exploit security vulnerabilities. This is achieved by providing the agent with <strong>non-blocking interactive sessions</strong> and <strong>summarizers</strong> to manage long command outputs. The agent can use these tools to <strong>debug and connect to remote servers</strong>, allowing it to solve challenges that were previously unsolvable.",
